# CPU-only install path (SR-21, AM-66, AM-73).
#
# Required by `params.environment.cpu_install_path_required_for` -- analysis and
# demo. Those two need to run on a machine with no NVIDIA GPU (a marker laptop,
# a CI runner, the Streamlit host), and neither trains anything.
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-cpu.in --generate-hashes --emit-index-url \
#       --index-strategy unsafe-best-match -o requirements-cpu.lock
#
# Torch and torchvision come explicitly from PyTorch's official CPU index. The
# unsuffixed PyPI wheels are not a CPU-only guarantee: the original lock pulled
# cuda-bindings, cuda-toolkit and related distributions while calling itself
# CPU-only (AM-73).
#
# This path does NOT run the test suite. `tests/test_env.py::test_cuda_build`
# hard-asserts a CUDA build with no skip marker, on purpose (AM-23): an env var
# that disables it would be set once in a shell profile and silently disarm the
# only check that catches a CPU build on the training machine.

--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

# --- runtime stack (params.environment), CPU builds --------------------------
torch==2.13.0+cpu
torchvision==0.28.0+cpu
numpy==2.5.1
pillow==12.3.0
scikit-image==0.26.0
glymur==0.14.3
pytest==9.1.1

# --- spec tooling, same rationale as requirements.in (AM-65) -----------------
PyYAML==6.0.3

# OpenJPEG 2.5.4 is a system library, externally provisioned and verified
# (AM-75); no Python lockfile can install or hash it. Glymur is the pinned Python
# binding only.
